{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Guess who just got ba[Bm]ck today?
[C] Them wild-eyed boys that [Em]had been away.
[Bm] Hadn't changed, hadn't [Em]much to say.
[Am] But man, I still think [C/D]them cats are crazy.

[G] They were askin’ if [Bm]you were around,
[C] How you was, where [D#]you could be found.
[Bm] Told ’em you were livin’ [Em]downtown,
[Am] Drivin’ all the old men [C/D]crazy.
{end_of_verse}


