{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G] You know that chick that used [Bm]to dance a lot?
[C] Every night she’d be on the [Em]floor, shakin’ what she got.
[Bm] When I say she [Em]was cool she was red hot.
[Am] I mean, she was [C/D]steamin’!


[G] And that time over at J[Bm]ohnny’s place,
[C] Well, this chick got up [D#]and she slapped Johnny’s face.
[Bm] Man, we just fell [Em]about the place.
[Am] If that chick don’t want to know, [C/D]forget her.
{end_of_verse}


